<article class="env-lemma" id="0GJD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GJD">Lemma <span data-tag="0GJD">59.84.2</span>.</a> Let $\Lambda $ be a Noetherian ring, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, let $f : X \to Y$ be a finite morphism of separated finite type schemes over $k$ of dimension $\leq 1$, and let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\Lambda $-modules on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. If $H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F})$ is a finite $\Lambda $-module, then so is $H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(Y, f_*\mathcal{F})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Namely, we have $H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(X, \mathcal{F}) = H^ q_{\acute{e}tale}(Y, f_*\mathcal{F})$ by the vanishing of $R^ qf_*$ for $q > 0$ (Proposition <a href="/tag/03QP" data-tag="03QP">59.55.2</a>) and the Leray spectral sequence (Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/0733" data-tag="0733">21.14.6</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>